LAMMPS (7 Feb 2024 - Update 1)
# LAMMPS script for Morse particles with high alpha parameter
# Simulates a fluid starting from random configuration

# Initialization
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
dimension       3
boundary        p p p


variable        temp equal 2.0

# System definition
region          box block 0 30 0 30 0 30
create_box      1 box
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (30 30 30)
  1 by 2 by 5 MPI processor grid
create_atoms    1 random 5000 12345 box
Created 5000 atoms
  using lattice units in orthogonal box = (0 0 0) to (30 30 30)
  create_atoms CPU = 0.002 seconds

# Set mass
mass            1 1.0

# Morse potential parameters
# U(r) = D0 * [exp(-2*alpha*(r-r0)) - 2*exp(-alpha*(r-r0))]
# High alpha parameter for gel-like behavior
pair_style      morse 2.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 30.0 1.0

# Initial velocity (low temperature for stability)
velocity        all create ${temp} 87287 dist gaussian
velocity        all create 2 87287 dist gaussian

# Neighbor list settings
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 10 delay 0 check yes

# Energy minimization to remove overlaps
minimize        1.0e-4 1.0e-6 1000 10000
Switching to 'neigh_modify every 1 delay 0 check yes' setting during minimization
Generated 0 of 0 mixed pair_coeff terms from geometric mixing rule
